## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical, beginner-friendly data erasure controls across accounts with auditable trails.

## Key Concepts

- S3 bucket versioning and Object Lock in Governance mode
- Cross-account Step Functions / IAM roles
- KMS CMK rotation and per-tenant keys
- CloudTrail Lake for immutable audit logs
- Access revocation via policy updates and least privilege

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: trigger erasure workflow
if (erasureRequested(tenantId)) {
  stepFunctions.startExecution({
    input: { tenantId }
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this with minimal tenant impact?
- How do you handle backups and replication to ensure complete erasure?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant isolation in a multi-account AWS data platform using modern controls (S3 Access Points, ABAC, cross-account roles) and an automated containment workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant S3 Access Points and isolated buckets
- ABAC with aws:PrincipalTag for tenant isolation
- Cross-account roles for analytics with least privilege
- Automated containment: CMK rotation, token revocation, data quarantine
- Immutable logging and breach test planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Conceptual IAM policy snippet for per-tenant access via ABAC
const policy = {
  Version: "2012-10-17",
  Statement: [
    {
      Effect: "Allow",
      Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      Resource: [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket-${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
      ],
      Condition: {
        StringEquals: {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

